{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":630,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:2Chr.4","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"2 Chronicles","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"2 Chronicles 4","reference":"2 Chronicles 4","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"The brazen altar, sea and lavers, ver."},{"verse":2,"text":"1-5."},{"verse":3,"text":"The golden candlesticks and tables, ver."},{"verse":4,"text":"7, 8."},{"verse":5,"text":"The doors overlaid with brass, the vessels of the altar, and other brass work, ver."},{"verse":6,"text":"9-18."},{"verse":7,"text":"The golden altar of incense with its appurtenances, ver."},{"verse":8,"text":"19-22."},{"verse":9,"text":"7.","scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":10,"text":"Their form - The old form which God prescribed to Moses.","scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":11,"text":"8.","scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":12,"text":"Ten tables - Whereon the shew-bread was set, ver.","scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":13,"text":"19.","scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":14,"text":"Perhaps each of these had twelve loaves on it.","scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":15,"text":"As the house was enlarged, so was the provision.","scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":16,"text":"16.","scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":17,"text":"His father - He is so called because Solomon usually called him by that name out of that great respect which he bare to him for his excellent art and service which he did for him: it being usual to call great artists and inventors of things by this name.","scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":18,"text":"20.","scriptureVerseStart":20,"scriptureVerseEnd":20},{"verse":19,"text":"The manner - According to the prescription of God to Moses.","scriptureVerseStart":20,"scriptureVerseEnd":20},{"verse":20,"text":"22.","scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22},{"verse":21,"text":"Of gold - In part; they were made of wood, but covered with golden plates.","scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":4}}